{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_533c81dd384a202572178406512950b400861323cee51997ca4c6a69a627fce7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The harness requires a provider API key (e.g. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY); Claude subscription login is not a supported auth path, and claw-analog selects providers by model and environment variables."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b63bdd1252f44f770530105f49c0abbb4468ec8bede2531f73554ade123d25a2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README instructs building from source via `cargo build --workspace` in rust/, warns against `cargo install claw-code` (a deprecated stub), and says to run `cargo test --workspace` after verifying the binary."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cc0ca2b1acb13829948672687f021a4f5a2398436377757e0d766360e323ebc3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states claw-code does not yet ship an ACP/Zed daemon or JSON-RPC entrypoint; `claw acp serve` is only a discoverability alias returning status with exit code 0, with real ACP support tracked in the roadmap."}],"claim_ids":["clm_533c81dd384a202572178406512950b400861323cee51997ca4c6a69a627fce7","clm_b63bdd1252f44f770530105f49c0abbb4468ec8bede2531f73554ade123d25a2","clm_cc0ca2b1acb13829948672687f021a4f5a2398436377757e0d766360e323ebc3"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:20:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_008bcd2bf2e842b3ad6af2cc9950a622","id":"pg_4a34626b043058229c0e62c897fb4447","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/ultraworkers-claw-code-readme-md-08106b0c3771-62c897fb4447.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_523a9c1b71a3574b89f93a961d79cb7d"],"title":"ultraworkers/claw-code/README.md @ 08106b0c3771","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:20:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_008bcd2bf2e842b3ad6af2cc9950a622"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:20:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_008bcd2bf2e842b3ad6af2cc9950a622","id":"pg_4f79405d9d545ef2b30e7b4eca3629ec","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/ultraworkers-claw-code-parity-md-08106b0c3771-7b4eca3629ec.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_626ea9c558465167a64a72fcc51bca97"],"title":"ultraworkers/claw-code/PARITY.md @ 08106b0c3771","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:20:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_008bcd2bf2e842b3ad6af2cc9950a622"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_27fb9b7b9870be1372716dbbee667b3005fdc2cd0a72ba2618c32c9873d04939"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Heavy indexing and embedding storage are deliberately kept out of claw-analog; the agent only calls retrieval over HTTP so the vector store and embedding secrets can be scaled or changed independently."},{"claim_ids":["clm_45ee35485f6fb08a9641f7fdbf320af99e88e35f867ef8d8b5e0bbd13b749fb8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Rust workspace contains the main `claw` CLI (rusty-claude-cli), an `api` crate for provider clients and streaming, a `runtime` crate with sessions and permission policy/enforcer, a `tools` crate, `claw-analog`, and `claw-rag-service`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6c92e9683047e7cc46371c8efb77ae3c8a9fdc89743ad0b7a5f5546bad0378ee"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"claw-analog supports --output-format json emitting NDJSON on stdout for scripts and CI, --stream for SSE streaming, and explicit limits such as --max-turns (default 24), --max-read-bytes (262144), and glob/grep caps."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ab162e8dc66e92a32ac979db517974f05fa7fa925f586657879566d9a5b12804"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"claw-analog enforces a canonical workspace root with relative paths, no `..`, and symlink/canonicalize containment checks; a PermissionPolicy and PermissionEnforcer gate tools, and dangerous modes are blocked in non-interactive runs unless explicitly accepted."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b59504dbc6a2e2fc2c5b091b4799ff2ae0f423adfcf2c99403f04520f9ca65fb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The main `claw` CLI is described as a full agent with a REPL, OAuth, an extended toolset including bash, MCP and plugins, streaming, and integration with Anthropic, OpenAI-compatible, and xAI providers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c3d8e4b253000de701b7c2fc4ab91385f78dcb218ff881074ae495b0471d9843"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"claw-analog is a lean agent on the same API layer with a narrow filesystem-only toolset (read_file, list_dir, glob_workspace, grep_workspace, git_diff, git_log, optional write_file and retrieve_context) and no arbitrary shell, MCP, or plugins."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f9faca4de03ad88168dcc7b9fdfda5a72ca44e8f2328f8aad9de107c44c51907"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"claw-rag-service is a separate process that indexes a repository into SQLite chunks plus embeddings and exposes an HTTP API with routes including /, /health, /v1/stats, and /v1/query, plus a minimal web UI."}],"claim_ids":["clm_27fb9b7b9870be1372716dbbee667b3005fdc2cd0a72ba2618c32c9873d04939","clm_45ee35485f6fb08a9641f7fdbf320af99e88e35f867ef8d8b5e0bbd13b749fb8","clm_6c92e9683047e7cc46371c8efb77ae3c8a9fdc89743ad0b7a5f5546bad0378ee","clm_ab162e8dc66e92a32ac979db517974f05fa7fa925f586657879566d9a5b12804","clm_b59504dbc6a2e2fc2c5b091b4799ff2ae0f423adfcf2c99403f04520f9ca65fb","clm_c3d8e4b253000de701b7c2fc4ab91385f78dcb218ff881074ae495b0471d9843","clm_f9faca4de03ad88168dcc7b9fdfda5a72ca44e8f2328f8aad9de107c44c51907"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:20:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_008bcd2bf2e842b3ad6af2cc9950a622","id":"pg_95fadcd50e055ba4bc3e5ba832257289","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/ultraworkers-claw-code-concept-md-08106b0c3771-5ba832257289.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_99a905feba42511ba6fb11182ff62324"],"title":"ultraworkers/claw-code/concept.md @ 08106b0c3771","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:20:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_008bcd2bf2e842b3ad6af2cc9950a622"}
